OL,3,GNEWSAHow the weather in space can
OL,4,Aaffect us on Earth - and the team
OL,5,Atrying to protect us
OL,6,
OL,7,FAt the Met Office headquarters, the
OL,8,Fscreens in one corner of the control
OL,9,Fcentre are focussed on close up imagery
OL,10,Fof the Sun.
OL,12,FIt is here that a space weather
OL,13,Fprediction team, one of only a small
OL,14,Fnumber worldwide, operates 24-hours a
OL,15,Fday, 365 days a year.
OL,17,FThe weather in space has the potential
OL,18,Fto impact our lives here on Earth in a
OL,19,Ffundamental way. GPS, power grids and
OL,20,Fsatellites are some of the vital
OL,21,Ftechnologies vulnerable to changes in
OL,22,Fthe earth's magnetic field.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,440,430,260,140,0,100
